# Featured leads (index pages)

## Projects (`/projects`)

Layout order: **Hero → Filter → Featured lead → filtered grid**.

1. **Filter first** — involvement / IP pills sit above the full-width lead.
2. **Lead follows involvement** — each involvement tab has a fixed featured project (via `getProjectsFeaturedLead(activeInvolvement)`). Do not auto-pick from sort order or “most recent”.
3. **Deduplicate from grid** — exclude the lead’s slug from the masonry / filter results. It only appears once as the full-width lead.
4. **Only change a lead** when the user **explicitly** asks to replace which project is featured for that involvement.

### Sources of truth (`PROJECTS_FEATURED_LEAD_BY_INVOLVEMENT`)

| Filter | Featured lead |
|--------|----------------|
| **All** / **End-to-End** | Dragon Age Writing Bundle |
| **Project Contribution** | Horizon Zero Dawn The Thunderjaw Collection Statue |
| **Specialized Services** | The Elder Scrolls Online 10-Year Coin Shadowbox (interim until user picks another) |

Home page (`projectsFeaturedLead`) stays the **All / End-to-End** lead (Dragon Age Writing Bundle).

## Insights (`/thoughts`)

Featured lead stays **above** the filter and is **not** filter-driven (`INSIGHTS_FEATURED_LEAD_SLUG` / `getInsightsFeaturedLead()`). Currently **When Game Merchandise Needs More Than Just a Logo**. Only change when the user explicitly asks.

## Do not

- Auto-pick a new lead from filter matches, shuffle, or “most recent”
- Show the same project again in the filtered grid after it already appears as the featured lead
- Move the Projects lead back above the filter without an explicit ask
- Change Insights to filter-driven leads without an explicit ask
